From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Mihalicka <tomas@mihalicka.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:41:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Model the payment lifecycle

Start the payments service with its domain model. A payment belongs to
one tenant, carries the client's idempotency key and an operation key
that the provider deduplicates charges on, and moves from pending to
succeeded or declined.

A submission the provider never answers leaves the payment unknown
rather than failed, because the charge may have gone through. An
unknown payment can be submitted again, and since the operation key
stays with the payment, the provider charges it at most once. A settled
payment refuses any further outcome.

Areas: domain
